1. **`main()` Function:**
   - `width`: The width of the rectangle.
   - `height`: The height of the rectangle.
   - `rectangle`: A `std::vector` containing the coordinates of the vertices of the rectangle.
   - `grid`: A `std::vector` containing the coordinates of the grid cells.
   - `j`: A `std::pair` (using `std::pair` to represent a row and column).
   - `equation`: A `std::string` that represents the shape of the rectangle. The `equation` is `std::string`, which represents the shape of the rectangle.
   - `rectangle[j]`: The coordinates of the first cell in the rectangle.
   - `grid[i]`: The coordinates of the second cell in the rectangle.
   - `area`: The area of the rectangle.
   - `insertionPoint(j)`: The position of the line to insert the shaded area.
   - `insertionPoint(j+1)`: The position of the line to insert the shaded area.
   - `return 0`: Indicates that the program has executed successfully.

2. **The Rectangle and its Shaded Portion:**
   - The `insertionPoint(j)` is the position of the line to insert the shaded area.
   - `insertionPoint(j+1)` is the position of the line to insert the shaded area.
   - `rectangle[j]`: The coordinates of the first cell in the rectangle.
   - `grid[j]`: The coordinates of the second cell in the rectangle.
   - `area = rectangle.size() - 1`:  The area of the rectangle is the difference between the first and second coordinates.
   - `std::cout << "  " << rectangle[i] << " " << grid[i] << std::endl;`: The area of the rectangle is the rectangle itself.
   - `std::cout << "Area of shaded region: " << area << " pixels"`:  The area of the shaded region is the area of the rectangle minus the area of the shaded portion.
   - `return area`: Returns the calculated area.

